condition_name: Dental Caries
condition_slug: dental-caries
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: A progressive breakdown of teeth exposed to the carbohydrate and bacterial plaque
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: Clinical Features of Dental Caries
    features[3]: Cavity formation in affected tooth,Starts as a white spot,Pain on exposure of the cavity to thermal changes or food particles
investigations[4]: Periapical radiographs,Bitewing radiographs,Electric pulp testers,Thermal test
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[3]: "Excision of lesion followed by: Amalgam filling, Glass Ionomer Cement (GIC) composite and Atraumatic Restorative Technique (ART) for enamel caries","Amalgam filling, GIC for dentine caries","Root Canal Therapy, pulp capping pulpotomy, pulpectomy for pulpal involvement"
  drug[1]: "Analgesics pre-operatively: paracetamol 1g 4-6 hourly orally to a maximum of 4 g daily"
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[0]:
complications[1]: Pulpitis; If not treated can cause apical periodontitis and dento alveolar abscess
prevention[5]: Oral health education,Regular scaling and polishing,Systemic and topical fluoride application,Fissure sealants,Routine dental check-ups
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null